window.DEVLOG.agents["d3_look"] = {"name": "Look dev & post", "role": "Car paint/glass/chrome materials, liveries, lighting rigs, bloom/tonemap/DOF post", "status": "done", "progress": 100, "current": "Fix round 2 done: closed-cabin glass (no more convertibles), car-mask speed blur (rival + player sharp, no bubble), chroma clamp", "done": ["API v1 posted", "materials.ts: paint (solid/metallic/pearl/candy/matte, clearcoat over LOD-blended object-space flake, base specular under coat), autoFinish, glass/lens (premultiplied Fresnel), chrome/blackChrome/brushedMetal/rubber/plastic/carbon (triplanar), lights, brakeDisc/caliper/rimMaterial/grille, interior/plate/badge, disposeObject", "Liveries: applyLivery projects a 5-view atlas in body space (no UVs): stripes/flames/checker/split/pinstripe/door roundels + all 8 paragon liveries; verified on real muscle (Stallion) + tuner bodies", "lighting.ts: raceLighting (texel-snapped follow shadow, key/fill/rim/hemi, night PMREM fallback), studioLighting (softbox PMREM, reflective floor + shadow catcher + cyclorama), contactShadow", "post.ts: HDR (MSAA on high) -> user passes -> GTAO -> speed blur -> bokeh DOF -> bloom chain -> ACES (hue-preserving blend) + grade/vignette/CA/grain -> SMAA/FXAA; presets + gradePreset", "Perf @1280x720, Apple A18 Pro (ANGLE Metal), post cost over a raw render: low ~+0.5ms, medium ~+1.6ms, high ~+3.9ms (GTAO ~1.6, MSAA4 ~1.2); DOF+speed blur +0.6ms (low/med) / +2.8ms (high)", "POLISH: AO now applied by post.ts itself (GTAO denoised output) and faded out with view depth 45-100 m: strip aerial/track banding gone; post.setAO({intensity, fadeNear, fadeFar})", "POLISH: studio blob on raked windshields/flat hoods was the radial-glow SIDE softboxes; all studio softboxes are now hard-cored strip lights (crisp streaks). Glass: viewer-facing normal (robust to flipped winding), direct-light glint x0.15, envMapIntensity 0.7; carbon clearcoat a bit rougher", "POLISH: DOF uses camera-to-surface distance (not view-axis depth), an in-focus band of max(0.4 m, 22% of focus), consistent px units: aperture 0.18 keeps the whole car sharp", "FEEL R1: speed blur mask rewritten: strength clamp(near/dist, 0.2, 1) (near 9 m), 0 for sky (depth>=0.9999) and skyline (fades out 400-900 m), car protected by screen ellipse + depth band (+/-3.5..5 m), taps landing on the car rejected (no ghosting). Verified on the hellkat race: near boards/lane/canopy lights stream, stars stay crisp", "FEEL R1: chromatic aberration is a speed cue: race grade base 0.2; post.setChroma(k) per frame; until called it auto-follows blur (0.2 + 1.4*blurK)", "FEEL R1: car paint envMapIntensity 1.5, base specular 0.7, direct-light glints x1.4 only when env's stadium lights are patched in (race); studio unchanged (checked compact/stallion/hellkat)", "R2 GLASS: glass writes depth (smoke can't paint over it), Fresnel floor 0.10, tint #0e1216, head-on opacity side 0.47 / raked windshield 0.62 / rear-facing backlight 0.66 + tint #07090c (auto-detected per pane from its car-space normal, or glass({rear:true})), env 1.5, light glints x0.35; modeler opacity hints are floored. Interior albedo x0.55, env 0.3-0.4, seat sheen 0.15. Paint base-colour luminance capped (0.5 saturated .. 0.75 white)", "R2 BLUR: CAR_MASK_LAYER (7) exported from post.ts; meshes on it render into a half-res distance+coverage mask (materials swapped + their render hooks muted for the pass, non-mesh objects hidden, any failure -> ellipse fallback); blur leaves both cars sharp and drops taps on them; ellipse/depth path kept as fallback. Chroma clamped at 0.65"], "todo": [], "notes": "R2: @core CAR_MASK_LAYER works with your world.ts traverse (verified in the race: stock seed 49 rival crisp at 126 km/h). The mask pass costs one extra half-res car-only render while blur is on; it rescans the layer every 30 frames (post.setScene forces a rescan). @carsA @carsB @carsC no glass edits needed: rear panes are detected from the pane's body-space normal (keep glass geometry authored in body space); glass({rear:true}) forces it. @cine NEW setSpeedBlur opts: ellipse {cx, cy, rx, ry} in UV with ORIGIN BOTTOM-LEFT (u = ndc.x*0.5+0.5, v = ndc.y*0.5+0.5; rx/ry = half-extents in UV, pad the projected car box ~15%), depth = camera-to-CAR-CENTRE distance in m (Euclidean), near (optional, default 9). Please add director.blur.ellipse + director.blur.depth. Legacy `protect` still works as a fallback (fixed ellipse 0.5,0.36,0.17,0.2 and depth = protect-3). @core world.ts:670 -> c.setSpeedBlur(b.k, { dir: b.dir, radial: b.radial, center: b.center, ellipse: b.ellipse, depth: b.depth }); and per frame c.setChroma(0.2 + 0.6 * director.fxK.speed + 0.3 * director.fxK.nitro) (until you call it, CA follows blur k automatically). POLISH DONE. @cine setFocus(dist, aperture): dist is camera-to-subject distance (Euclidean), the whole car stays sharp within max(0.4, 0.22*dist) m of it; aperture 0.15-0.3 = subtle background blur, 0.5+ = strong. @env AO fades out between 45 and 100 m view depth (post.setAO({fadeNear, fadeFar}) to tune). @show @carsC studio env is now strip lights (overhead x4 + side strips); no API change. Debug: studioEnvMap(renderer, {omit:[...]}) / look.html?envomit=top,side,side2,rim,card,dome,floor. DONE. API (stable): see previous notes; additions: Grade.huePreserve (0..1, default 0.55: stops red paint going pink under ACES), POST_PRESETS export, rig.fit(Box3|Object3D). @kit pass applyLivery(build, spec, {atlas: quality==='low' ? 1024 : 2048}); a car's livery handle must be disposed with the car. @carsA compact.ts currently throws in _helpersA resample (look.html?body=compact falls back): 'Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 0)' at _helpersA.ts:1006. @carsA @carsB @carsC please set build.body.userData = {belt, sill, door:[xR,xF], cowl} so stripes/roundels sit on the right lines (defaults: belt 62% of paint height). @core @show perf numbers above are the post cost only; the high preset's GTAO can be dropped first if the race scene is over budget (POST_PRESETS.high.ao=false). Lookdev: /src/render/three/dev/look.html?rig=race|studio&view=spheres|car|side|rear|close|top|front&body=<real body>&livery=&number=&paragon=&finish=&dof=d,a&blur=k&radial=1&quality=&perf=1&nolights=1&noenv=1", "etaMinutes": 0, "updated": "2026-10-24T10:17:40Z"};
